    "body": "released: lane limit, the red-main fix #3337 takes the slot. Held work: branch `issue/2620-gpu-compute-seam` at 9b58a77be3333ffaf7a3dcc0762f992bd1992a11, worktree `.claude/worktrees/issue-917`.\n\n- Done: `origin/main` (7a626a7f5) is merged into the branch with no conflicts (merge commit 4f49e2aed). The decision entry `docs/decisions/2620-gpu-compute-seam.md` already covers the one edge `camcraft-ui -> camcraft-gpu` (six items). The wip commit has two changes: the `Cargo.lock` version bump of `camcraft-gpu` to 0.25.0, and a fix to `xtask/src/heavy_plan_tests.rs` (`reach_follows_the_crate_dependencies`). That test is new on main. The kernel no longer reaches every crate, because `gpu` has no `camcraft-*` dependency.\n- Next: run `cargo test -p xtask` (it was stopped before a result), `cargo test -p camcraft-gpu`, `gpu_parity_fixture_matches_the_grid` in `camcraft-motion`, and clippy for `camcraft-gpu`. Then run the quick gate (batch plan) and `cargo xtask gate heavy --base main --dry-run`. Then open the draft PR with `Process change: yes` (xtask changed), the new direct `wgpu =30.0.1` dependency named, `Fixes #2620` and `Refs #3336`.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
